<Project>
  <!--
    The plug-and-play scenarios stand for a user's fresh folder, so MSBuild's upward search stops
    here, and tests/scenarios' settings (TreatWarningsAsErrors, the package output folder) do not
    reach the projects the templates create. Their build steps check " 0 Warning(s)" instead, and
    the ASM0013 steps see a warning, not an error.

    The one setting: NuGet's vulnerability audit is off. The templates pin xunit's packages, and
    an advisory published later against one of them would add a warning (NU1901-NU1904) to a
    build that changed nothing; tests/scenarios keeps those warnings from being errors for the
    same reason, but here every warning counts.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <NuGetAudit>false</NuGetAudit>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
